-1569048.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Do something. You can’t die like this': flydubai pilot Capt Smit Machchar recounts cockpit attack]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/do-something-you-cant-die-like-this-flydubai-pilot-capt-smit-machchar-recounts-cockpit-attack/articleshow/135019095.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135019095.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/do-something-you-cant-die-like-this-flydubai-pilot-capt-smit-machchar-recounts-cockpit-attack/articleshow/135019095.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/do-something-you-cant-die-like-this-flydubai-pilot-capt-smit-machchar-recounts-cockpit-attack/articleshow/135019095.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T23:55:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manju V</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135019137,imgsize-224188.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['He kept on hitting': Indian flydubai pilot Smit Machchhar reveals what happened mid-flight as he was stabbed]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-kept-on-hitting-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-reveals-what-happened-mid-flight-as-he-was-stabbed/articleshow/135018356.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135018356.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Smit Machchhar was attacked by his co-pilot during a routine Flydubai flight, which he initially misinterpreted. As he attempted to defend himself, he lost consciousness amidst his desperate fight for survival. Other crew members intervened and helped regain control of the aircraft after he opened the cockpit door. The pilot expressed gratitude for the medical treatment he received after safely landing in Saudi Arabia.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-kept-on-hitting-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-reveals-what-happened-mid-flight-as-he-was-stabbed/articleshow/135018356.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-kept-on-hitting-indian-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-reveals-what-happened-mid-flight-as-he-was-stabbed/articleshow/135018356.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T23:20:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135018586,imgsize-94948.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['AIADMK would welcome Dhanush with both hands', says Rajendra Balaji]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aiadmk-would-welcome-dhanush-with-both-hands-says-rajendra-balaji/articleshow/135018032.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135018032.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During a recent press conference, AIADMK leader K T Rajendra Balaji expressed enthusiasm about actor Dhanush possibly entering politics. He mentioned that the party would gladly accept Dhanush's involvement, highlighting the significant appeal actors like him have over the youth. Additionally, it was observed that Dhanush has rebranded his fan club to align with his evolving public persona, showcasing his readiness for greater engagement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aiadmk-would-welcome-dhanush-with-both-hands-says-rajendra-balaji/articleshow/135018032.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aiadmk-would-welcome-dhanush-with-both-hands-says-rajendra-balaji/articleshow/135018032.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T23:00:23+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135018223,imgsize-57497.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Thoughts with those who have lost their loved ones': PM Modi on Kolkata stampede]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thoughts-with-those-who-have-lost-their-loved-ones-pm-modi-on-kolkata-stampede/articleshow/135017835.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135017835.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The incident occurred around 7.40 pm in the Girish Park police station area amid heavy crowds of pandal visitors and rainfall. As rain began, people waiting outside the pandal rushed forward, causing some to fall on the road and triggering a stampede, a senior police officer told PTI. All the injured were rescued and taken to Calcutta Medical College for treatment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thoughts-with-those-who-have-lost-their-loved-ones-pm-modi-on-kolkata-stampede/articleshow/135017835.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thoughts-with-those-who-have-lost-their-loved-ones-pm-modi-on-kolkata-stampede/articleshow/135017835.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T22:57:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135018051,imgsize-911375.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kolkata Durga Puja Stampede: 19 dead; PM Modi, Amit Shah, Rahul Gandhi, Mamata Banerjee express grief]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-durga-puja-stampede-pm-modi-amit-shah-mamata-express-grief/articleshow/135017733.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135017733.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a heartbreaking incident at a Durga Puja pandal in north Kolkata, a stampede claimed the lives of at least 19 people and left 25 others injured amid a surge of visitors driven by panic from heavy rains. Rescue efforts were promptly initiated, and medical staff rushed the injured to hospitals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-durga-puja-stampede-pm-modi-amit-shah-mamata-express-grief/articleshow/135017733.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-durga-puja-stampede-pm-modi-amit-shah-mamata-express-grief/articleshow/135017733.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T22:52:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135017840,imgsize-68846.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sabarimala temple opens for Thulam month rituals; CM Satheesan offers prayers]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sabarimala-temple-opens-for-thulam-month-rituals-cm-satheesan-offers-prayers/articleshow/135016954.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135016954.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The revered Sabarimala Lord Ayyappa temple was opened on Saturday for the rituals of the Thulam month, drawing numerous devotees eager to pay their respects. Kerala Chief Minister V D Satheesan, along with other esteemed guests, visited the shrine for prayers. The temple's opening for devotees is scheduled for 5 am on Sunday, coinciding with Mahanavami and Vijayadashami, a unique occurrence in many decades.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sabarimala-temple-opens-for-thulam-month-rituals-cm-satheesan-offers-prayers/articleshow/135016954.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sabarimala-temple-opens-for-thulam-month-rituals-cm-satheesan-offers-prayers/articleshow/135016954.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T22:36:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135017615,imgsize-100056.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kolkata pandal stampede: Heavy rush amid rain led to deadly incident - top developments]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-pandal-stampede-heavy-rush-amid-rain-led-to-deadly-incident-top-developments/articleshow/135017310.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135017310.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A chaotic stampede unfolded at the Sarada Park Durga Puja pandal in north Kolkata due to a crowd surge, leading to at least 1 deaths and 15 injuries. Emergency services transported the injured to Calcutta Medical College and Hospital for immediate medical assistance. The West Bengal health minister, alongside other political leaders, responded by visiting the scene and the hospital.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-pandal-stampede-heavy-rush-amid-rain-led-to-deadly-incident-top-developments/articleshow/135017310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kolkata-pandal-stampede-heavy-rush-amid-rain-led-to-deadly-incident-top-developments/articleshow/135017310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T22:28:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135017470,imgsize-2050862.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tamil Nadu BJP slams ministers for allowing Muslim aide in skull cap into temple]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tamil-nadu-bjp-slams-ministers-for-allowing-muslim-aide-in-skull-cap-into-temple/articleshow/135017190.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135017190.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The BJP alleged that the incident, which took place on Saturday, went against a Madras high court order issued in January 2024 that restricts non-Hindus from proceeding beyond the temple’s flagmast unless they submit an undertaking affirming their faith in the deity and their willingness to follow Hindu customs. The party also claimed that the entry violated the temple’s dress code and religious traditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tamil-nadu-bjp-slams-ministers-for-allowing-muslim-aide-in-skull-cap-into-temple/articleshow/135017190.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tamil-nadu-bjp-slams-ministers-for-allowing-muslim-aide-in-skull-cap-into-temple/articleshow/135017190.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T22:15:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135017265,imgsize-68250.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Taking away right to vote, protest’: Uddhav backs opposition's ‘regime change’ call against government]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/taking-away-right-to-vote-protest-uddhav-backs-oppositions-regime-change-call-against-government/articleshow/135017025.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135017025.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/taking-away-right-to-vote-protest-uddhav-backs-oppositions-regime-change-call-against-government/articleshow/135017025.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/taking-away-right-to-vote-protest-uddhav-backs-oppositions-regime-change-call-against-government/articleshow/135017025.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T21:57:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135017055,imgsize-151444.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NCB busts two synthetic drug labs in Greater Noida, seizes drugs worth Rs 50 crore]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncb-busts-two-synthetic-drug-labs-in-greater-noida-seizes-drugs-worth-rs-50-crore/articleshow/135016626.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135016626.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Narcotics Control Bureau conducted a significant raid on two synthetic-drug laboratories in Greater Noida. During the operation, authorities seized large quantities of Methamphetamine and precursor chemicals. Two individuals were arrested, including a Nigerian national using a false identity. Investigators are tracing financial and chemical supply networks linked to the suspects. Citizens are urged to report suspicious activities to promote public safety and environmental health.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncb-busts-two-synthetic-drug-labs-in-greater-noida-seizes-drugs-worth-rs-50-crore/articleshow/135016626.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncb-busts-two-synthetic-drug-labs-in-greater-noida-seizes-drugs-worth-rs-50-crore/articleshow/135016626.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T21:32:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135016757,imgsize-83850.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Supreme Court’s enquiry committee launches complaint portal over violence during July protests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-courts-enquiry-committee-launches-complaint-portal-over-violence-during-july-protests/articleshow/135016581.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135016581.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A complaint portal has been launched by the High Powered Enquiry Committee for individuals affected by protests. This portal allows victims to confidentially submit their complaints regarding violence that occurred in July. The Ministry of Home Affairs stated that submissions can also be made in person or via post. The committee will prioritize cases involving serious violence, especially against women protesters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-courts-enquiry-committee-launches-complaint-portal-over-violence-during-july-protests/articleshow/135016581.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-courts-enquiry-committee-launches-complaint-portal-over-violence-during-july-protests/articleshow/135016581.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T21:14:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135016594,imgsize-191442.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man killed, four injured in suspected militant attack on Kuki village in Manipur]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/man-killed-four-injured-in-suspected-militant-attack-on-kuki-village-in-manipur/articleshow/135015831.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135015831.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A tragic incident unfolded in Chassad village, Manipur, where a militant attack led to the death of one man and injuries to four others. Gunfire erupted between the militants and a local armed faction, with the violence persisting into the evening. Emergency services promptly transported the injured to a hospital, but sadly, one victim did not survive.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/man-killed-four-injured-in-suspected-militant-attack-on-kuki-village-in-manipur/articleshow/135015831.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/man-killed-four-injured-in-suspected-militant-attack-on-kuki-village-in-manipur/articleshow/135015831.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T20:11:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135016003,imgsize-170558.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman journalist, who accused Rahul Gandhi of manhandling, files complaint against him, others]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/woman-journalist-who-accused-rahul-gandhi-of-manhandling-files-complaint-against-him-others/articleshow/135015636.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135015636.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Richa Parasar has alleged mistreatment, threats and use of criminal force against her while she was reporting on a protest near the Supreme Court on October 12, 2026. Parashar, who said she was three months pregnant, has alleged that Rahul Gandhi 'grabbed her hand' and 'pulled her' forward before his security personnel pushed her away while she was covering the INDIA bloc's protest against CEC Gyanesh Kumar on October 12.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/woman-journalist-who-accused-rahul-gandhi-of-manhandling-files-complaint-against-him-others/articleshow/135015636.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/woman-journalist-who-accused-rahul-gandhi-of-manhandling-files-complaint-against-him-others/articleshow/135015636.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-17T19:47:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135015767,imgsize-162623.cms"/></item></channel></rss>